eFTI Gate (EE) — Authors
========================

The eFTI Gate (EE) specification corpus is maintained by KeMIT —
Keskkonnaministeeriumi Infotehnoloogiakeskus (Estonia). Copyright and licence
remain with KeMIT (see LICENSE).

This file names the humans behind the work. It does not affect copyright,
licence terms, or the Contributor License Agreement (see CLA.md).

Architect and lead author
-------------------------

  Rainer Türner — KeMIT
    GitHub:  https://github.com/turnerrainer  (@turnerrainer)
    Email:   rainer.turner@gmail.com
    Reference architecture, specification corpus, contract artefacts
    (OpenAPI, DB schema, errors, logging, permissions, transformations),
    epics, diagrams, planning material, and editorial direction.

Predecessor procurement deliverable
-----------------------------------

  Askend Estonia OÜ
    Delivered the initial project analysis, first-pass epic set, and data
    model under public procurement. The surviving background material is
    preserved under docs/efti-analysis/; the full original deliverable is
    preserved on the kemit-ee/efti-gate-poc repository under the
    v0.2-askend-final tag.

Predecessor PoC
---------------

  Digilogistika Keskus
    Built the original eFTI Gate proof-of-concept that informed Askend's
    procurement-phase analysis. State preserved on the
    kemit-ee/efti-gate-poc repository under the
    v0.1-pikker-digilogistika-baseline tag.

Disclosure: AI assistance
-------------------------

Specification drafts were produced with assistance from Anthropic Claude
(claude.ai/code, Claude Code CLI). Per institutional policy and prevailing
authorship conventions, AI assistants are tools rather than authors:
human authors are responsible for the content, copyright and licence
remain with KeMIT, and contributors grant rights under the CLA.

Contact: help@kemit.ee
